Reducing the number of neighbors clearly speeds up $\cspsb$. However,
as there is no free lunch, it reduces the number of elements at
distance $r$, i.e., the volume of the Hamming balls. Apparently, the
favorable effect is stronger, and we can improve upon the running
time. Since we are altering the notion of neighbors and thus of 
distance, we should define everything formally.
