codex
The redesigned family passes the full local suite. At shipping size it has exactly 81 valid assignments among \(3^{80}\), random guessing hit 0/200,000, four in-context attacks are 0/8, and the recognized-system reference solves 8/8 at roughly 625,000 exact scalar operations per instance. The answer is 161 characters/80 atoms and the compact quadratic route is bounded at 250 operations. I’m testing the new ladder against the oracle pool now.
