codex
A final domain audit found one omission worth fixing: for a CSP, the standard attack is DPLL/unit propagation, not just Gaussian elimination after recognizing the hidden algebra. The native DPLL probe solves all nine tested shipping instances in five nodes, about 39–41 thousand exact checks each. I’m reporting that successful standard attack as `reference_algorithm` and retaining Gaussian elimination as the guaranteed polynomial comparison—an honest Track-B gap of roughly 39,000 mechanical checks versus 250 compact operations.
