   110	The witness is the paper's own satisfying assignment, and verify() checks every
   111	such clause directly. No finite-field instance is substituted for the CSP.
   112	
   113	Step-0 and track decision. The paper's main theorem gives a deterministic
   114	exponential algorithm for general (d,k)-CSP; at d=k=3 its displayed bound is
   115	about 2.077^n. That theorem is not an average-case lower bound for planted
   116	formulas, so this module makes no Track-A claim. Its promised distribution has
   117	an efficient specialized algorithm: recover the ternary-linear relation behind
   118	each complete forbidden-tuple block and run exact Gaussian elimination. The
   119	reference implementation and its measured field-operation count are reported
   120	under reference_algorithm, as Track B requires.
   121	
   122	Generation route. Variables carry distinct nonzero vectors of a base-3 vector
   123	space. The generator samples a quadratic monomial Q(v)=v_p*v_q, an affine
   124	linear form, and a constant, then samples the satisfying colors first. Every
   125	block is subsequently made from a two- or three-variable linear equation whose
   126	right side is evaluated on that planted assignment. A triangular set of core
   127	relations determines all non-basis variables from the basis variables, proving
   128	that exactly 3^q assignments satisfy the formula. Extra relations are sampled
   129	from the same vector-addition identity and are redundant. The certificate is
   130	therefore known by inverse generation, never by solving the produced formula.
   131	
   132	Compact route. For f(v)=v_p*v_q+L(v)+c over GF(3), the affine part cancels from
   133	f(u)+f(v)-f(u+v). Binary basis-doubling relations reveal c, while the basis-pair
   134	relations have one exceptional pair revealing p,q. Choosing L=0 then gives the
   135	valid assignment f(v)=v_p*v_q+c. At n=80 this is at most 240 per-coordinate
