/bin/bash -lc "nl -ba README.md | sed -n '1,260p'" in /home/gson/gvrepo/results/1005.4874
 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Quadratic-polarization witnesses for three-color CSP
     2	
     3	| Profile field | Value |
     4	|---|---|
     5	| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
     6	| Native domain | logic |
     7	| Object regime | finite discrete |
     8	| Computational core | CSP/SAT |
     9	| Certificate form | integer tuple (the paper's color assignment) |
    10	| Intended intuition | invariant: recognize polarized quadratic labels |
    11	| Domain essentiality | native |
    12	| Reduction | none |
    13	
    14	This generator uses the literal, constraint, formula, and assignment objects in
    15	Dominik Scheder's [*Using a Skewed Hamming Distance to Speed Up Deterministic
    16	Local Search*](https://arxiv.org/abs/1005.4874). A solver receives a native
    17	`(3,3)`-CSP: every displayed forbidden tuple is exactly one clause made from
    18	literals `(x_i != c)`. It must return any satisfying three-color assignment.
    19	`verify` checks the assignment's shape and evaluates every clause exactly; it
    20	never reads the planted answer.
    21	
    22	## Why this is Track B
    23	
    24	Section 1 fixes the CSP definition. Section 2 gives the paper's recursive
    25	Ball-CSP search, and Theorem 3.3 gives the directed-cycle deterministic bound;
    26	for the displayed `(3,3)` regime it is about `2.077^n poly(n)`. That is an upper
    27	bound, not evidence that a planted distribution is Track-A hard. This family
    28	therefore makes the narrower Track-B claim and openly exposes the algorithm
    29	that exists.
    30	
    31	The required domain-standard reference is native finite-domain DPLL with
    32	unit/functional propagation. It solves the promised shipping instance in five
    33	nodes, 39,489 exact checks, and 0.0057 s; across eight seeds it solves 8/8 in 40
    34	nodes, 321,169 checks, and 0.035 s. Its general worst case is exponential. A
    35	second, guaranteed polynomial algorithm recognizes each block as a linear row
    36	over `GF(3)` and applies dense exact Gaussian elimination in `O(B n^2)`. That
    37	route used 1,208,450 scalar field operations and 0.098 s on the shipping
    38	instance, and 10,800,467 operations/0.601 s across eight seeds.
    39	
    40	The compact route is different. Labels are base-3 vectors and the block
    41	constants are the polarization of `Q(v)=v_p v_q`. Affine terms cancel.
    42	Basis-doubling blocks identify the constant, one exceptional basis-pair block
    43	identifies `p,q`, and `Q(v)+c` is then a valid assignment. At shipping size this
    44	requires at most 250 exact multiply/add/reduce or comparison operations. Even
    45	the strongest measured native reference therefore needs about 39,000 checks
    46	against the compact route's 250 operations. The easy cases deliberately avoided are a visible triangular
    47	variable order (greedy propagation solved it) and a purely affine label rule
    48	(the obvious ansatz would solve it). The variables and blocks are now shuffled,
    49	and the planted function always has a genuine cross term.
    50	
    51	## Worked demo
    52	
    53	With `seed=1`, the complete demo is:
    54	
    55	```text
    56	SATISFY A THREE-COLOR CSP
    57	
    58	There are n=8 variables x0 through x7. Each color is 0, 1, or 2.
    59	A literal (x_i != c) is true exactly when x_i is not color c.
    60	A clause is an OR of its literals, and the formula is the AND of all clauses.
    61	
    62	Clauses are displayed in blocks. A forbidden tuple abc on scope [x_i,x_j,x_k]
    63	means (x_i != a) OR (x_j != b) OR (x_k != c). Binary scopes are analogous.
    64	
    65	Labels: x0=20 x1=11 x2=12 x3=02 x4=01 x5=21 x6=22 x7=10
    66	
    67	B0 [x4,x3] forbid: 10 22 01 12 00 21
    68	B1 [x7,x4,x1] forbid: 021 102 010 201 111 002 020 200 122 012 211 100 212 110 121 220 222 001
    69	B2 [x5,x4,x0] forbid: 000 010 221 012 021 211 101 111 102 001 220 120 200 212 110 122 022 202
    70	B3 [x7,x0] forbid: 01 00 10 22 12 21
    71	B4 [x6,x5,x7] forbid: 222 001 202 121 200 011 120 210 012 110 112 022 102 000 211 101 020 221
    72	B5 [x0,x6,x4] forbid: 122 220 101 202 212 102 012 120 111 001 000 021 211 110 200 010 221 022
    73	B6 [x5,x4,x6] forbid: 220 100 221 022 212 021 101 122 210 000 011 111 202 010 120 201 112 002
    74	B7 [x2,x4,x1] forbid: 102 212 222 011 200 221 022 121 020 010 002 120 111 201 100 001 112 210
    75	
    76	Return a JSON list of 8 colors in x0,...,x7 order inside <answer></answer>.
    77	```
    78	
    79	One answer is `<answer>[1,0,2,0,2,1,1,1]</answer>`.
    80	`verify(inst, inst["answer"])` returns `(True, "ok")`; dropping the last
    81	entry returns `(False, "assignment is too short: got 7, expected 8")`.
    82	There are nine valid demo assignments. A person can solve it on paper by
    83	recognizing each block's linear relation and using the two-digit labels; it is
    84	small enough to check all eight resulting colors directly.
    85	
    86	## Difficulty presets
    87	
    88	Measurements use `seed=20260905`; `hard` is the proposed shipping preset.
    89	
    90	| Preset | n | blocks | native clauses | valid assignments | reference operations | rendered chars |
    91	|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
    92	| demo | 8 | 8 | 120 | 9 | 5,157 | 1,731 |
    93	| easy | 50 | 160 | 2,844 | 81 | 235,743 | 17,009 |
    94	| medium | 80 | 320 | 5,712 | 81 | 622,510 | 33,115 |
    95	| **hard** | **80** | **640** | **11,472** | **81** | **1,208,450** | **64,677** |
    96	
    97	An earlier `n=26, B=60` easy draft was solved by one live oracle before the
    98	external quota was exhausted, so that rung was removed. Escalation doubles the
    99	number of redundant, same-distribution constraint blocks while keeping the
   100	80-color witness and 250-operation compact route fixed.
   101	
   102	## Gate results
   103	
   104	| Gate | Result | Measurement |
   105	|---|---|---|
   106	| G1 | pass | 12/12 planted witnesses verify |
   107	| G2 | pass | drop, swap, duplicate, empty, and out-of-range corruptions rejected with five distinct reasons |
   108	| G3 | pass | 12/12 tagged prose round trips; 12/12 JSON-native checks |
   109	| G4 | pass | exact fraction `3^-76`; 0/200,000 structure-aware uniform assignments valid |
   110	| G5 | pass | exactly 81 valid answers; DPLL 5 nodes/39,489 checks/0.0057 s; Gaussian 1,208,450 operations/0.098 s; all-affine attack 0/243 |
   111	| G6 | pass | five attacks each 0/8; native DPLL and polynomial elimination both 8/8 as expected |
   112	| G7 | pass | `n=160` builds; block escalation 640→1,280 keeps answer length fixed |
   113	| G8 | pass | 80/80 invariant keys, 80/80 carried witnesses, 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
   114	| G9(c) | pass | 161 chars, 41 estimated tokens, 80 atoms, 250 intended operations |
   115	
   116	The five failing attacks are per-variable forbidden-tuple frequency, sequential
   117	minimum-violation greedy, 256 uniform restarts, the by-hand digit-sum ansatz,
   118	and exhaustive affine label functions. The successful GF(3) reference solver
   119	is reported separately, as Track B requires.
   120	
   121	## Oracle loop and G9 arms
   122	
   123	The required harness was run, but the OpenRouter account reached its total key
   124	limit. Errors do not count as failed solver attempts, so **there is no external
   125	hardness verdict and this result must not be treated as shipped/hardened yet**.
   126	The fresh main transcript contains four independent redraw errors at the revised
   127	`easy` rung. All four happened to select the OpenAI endpoint before the retry
   128	budget was exhausted; the metadata still records the configured two-vendor
   129	pool. The authoritative next step is to rerun `harden.py` with a quota-enabled
   130	key, not to interpret 403s as model failures.
   131	
   132	| Preset | Seed | Model | Solved | Why |
   133	|---|---:|---|---|---|
   134	| easy | 1697072274 | GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 total key limit |
   135	| easy | 186881397 | GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 total key limit |
   136	| easy | 2085105980 | GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 total key limit |
   137	| easy | 1933100789 | GPT-5.6 Terra | error | HTTP 403 total key limit |
   138	
   139	| Arm | Solved/attempts | Errors | Conclusion |
   140	|---|---:|---:|---|
   141	| bare | 0/0 | 4 | unavailable: HTTP 403 total key limit |
   142	| structural | 0/0 | 4 | unavailable: HTTP 403 total key limit |
   143	| placebo | 0/0 | 4 | unavailable: HTTP 403 total key limit |
   144	
   145	`hinted - placebo` is undefined as an oracle effect (stored as `0.0` only
   146	because both denominators have zero scored attempts). The hint names only the
   147	polarization invariant; it does not give the recovery steps. The answer and
   148	route measurements remain 161 characters/80 atoms and 250 operations.
   149	
   150	## Use
   151	
   152	From the repository root:
   153	
   154	```python
   155	import importlib.util, json
   156	
   157	path = "results/1005.4874/gen_1005_4874.py"
   158	spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("g", path)
   159	g = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
   160	spec.loader.exec_module(g)
   161	
   162	inst = g.make_instance(seed=7, **g.DIFFICULTY[g.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY])
   163	text = g.render(inst)
   164	answer = g.parse_answer("<answer>" + json.dumps(inst["answer"]) + "</answer>")
   165	assert g.verify(inst, answer) == (True, "ok")
   166	```
   167	
   168	Emit records with `bash scripts/emit.sh 1005.4874 20 hard`. The module uses only
   169	the Python standard library and performs no file I/O, network access, or import-time
   170	printing.
   171	
   172	## Caveats
   173	
   174	- A CAS, SMT solver, or the included relation-recognition/Gaussian routine solves
   175	  this promised family efficiently. That is the Track-B baseline, not a failed
   176	  Track-A claim.
   177	- The exact `3^-76` density is under uniform length-80 ternary assignments. It
   178	  does not describe a solver that has recognized the quadratic invariant.
   179	- The panel includes native DPLL/unit propagation and exact specialized
   180	  Gaussian elimination, but not an external industrial SAT/SMT package;
   181	  solver-specific preprocessing behavior remains unmeasured.
   182	- `canonical_key` is invariant under the tested block/tuple reorderings, variable
   183	  renamings, and independent cyclic color translations. It canonically records
   184	  every block by its public base-3 label scope and omits only clause right sides,
   185	  which are interchangeable under the declared per-variable color translations.
   186	- The 64,677-character shipping statement is large. The answer and intended
   187	  arithmetic remain within G9(c), but a future audit should distinguish failure
   188	  to discover polarization from failure caused only by reading volume.
   189	- Most importantly, OpenRouter quota exhaustion prevented STEP 4 and the G9
   190	  diagnostic from producing scored attempts. Do not trust the hardness claim
   191	  until those artifacts are replaced by successful harness runs.

